NZFTC Employee Management System

Main_System data notes:
- Employee records are read from and written to `main/Main_System/Employee Management/Employee_Records`.
- Employer tax details are read from `main/Main_System/Employer_Details.txt`.
- Payslips are saved under `main/Main_System/Employee Management/Employee_Records/Payslips`.
  The folder is created automatically if it does not already exist.

Build:
- In VS Code, press `Ctrl+Shift+B` and choose:
  - `Build Main_System C++ app`
  - `Build NZFTC_EMS ASP.NET app`
- The C++ build needs the Visual Studio C++ workload installed.
- If the C++ task says MSVC is missing, open the repo from a Developer Command Prompt or install the C++ Build Tools.
- The ASP.NET build needs the .NET 10 SDK installed.

Runtime:
- The app now resolves data paths from the copied workspace automatically, so it does not depend on a separate `D:\MyApps\Apps for other Apps` folder.
- Folder structure: `main/Main_System/` contains all C++ backend code, `main/NZFTC_EMS/UI/` contains Qt UI files.
- Web authentication now calls the Main_System bridge executable (`main.exe`) with `--ui-bridge` commands.
- Build `main.exe` before running the ASP.NET app. You can override its path with `NZFTC_MAIN_SYSTEM_BRIDGE_EXE`.
